ing something.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Nigel</span>: I promise we'll go ziplining next time we have a school break. <br> <span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Great! I can't wait!", "type": "example"}, {"content": " You use the Future tense (with will) to make promises.<br/> For example: <span class=\"italic\">I'll do the dishes right away.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " You can also make a promise by using the words \"I promise\" before an action.<br/> For example: <span class=\"italic\">I promise to clean my room.</span><span class=\"italic\"> I promise I'll do the dishes right away.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " You can respond to promises with an expression like:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Great!<br/> I believe you.<br/> OK, no problem.<br/> That's fine.<br/> Thanks a lot!</span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "cottage ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small vacation home in a rural area", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Thanks for inviting me to this cottage.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le10ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about free time activities.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to laugh", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to react to a funny situation with sounds and body movement", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You make me laugh, Peter.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le10ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "bungee jumping", "type": "name"}, {"content": "activity of jumping from a high position holding a strong elastic rope", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I go bungee jumping on weekends.", "typ